==English==

===Etymology===
Cf. Old Norse {{term|meiða||to injure seriously, to hurt}}<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary|maim}}</ref>.

===Pronunciation===
*: {{rhymes|eɪm}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[wound]] seriously; to cause permanent loss of function of a limb or part of the body.

